    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "isiLQ",
      "x": 2900,
      "y": 3134,
      "name": "Note / Choose mode",
      "metadata": {
        "type": "note"
      },
      "fill": "#717171",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 340,
      "content": "FLOW CONTEXT · Access (choose a mode)\nSTATE: fresh install — no profile, no server, no database.\nWHY: this replaces the old cloud sign-up step; the storage model is the first decision.\nOPTIONS: Local only (SQLite in the app's sandbox) · Self-hosted (server URL + token).\nACTION: Continue → /setup/local or /setup/server. The choice is editable in Settings ▸ Server.\nOFFLINE: both paths work with the radio off — nothing on this screen calls the network.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "qC0aZ",
      "x": 3370,
      "y": 3134,
      "name": "Note / Connect server",
      "metadata": {
        "type": "note"
      },
      "fill": "#717171",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 340,
      "content": "FLOW CONTEXT · Access (connect server)\nINPUT: server URL (https or LAN host) + the invite token the host issued.\nCHECK: Test connection → GET /health; show reachability and API version inline, never a toast.\nFAILURE: timeout · bad token · http:// on a public host → inline error under the field, keep the typed value.\nSECURITY: the token goes to the device keychain; no analytics or remote fonts on this screen.\nEDGE: server reachable but household removed → offer to re-join with a new token.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "S9Unqp",
      "x": 3840,
      "y": 3134,
      "name": "Note / Server connected",
      "metadata": {
        "type": "note"
      },
      "fill": "#717171",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 340,
      "content": "FLOW CONTEXT · Access (server connected)\nSTATE: server verified, household resolved from the token.\nSHOWS: host, household name, API version — the three things support will ask for.\nACTION: Continue → Pantry with an empty household · 'Use a different server' → back to the form.\nCOPY: 'Connected' not 'Success' — it describes the state, not the tap.\nA11Y: the green check is paired with text; color is never the only signal.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
